<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Sullivan's Island</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">28 June 1776</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Sullivan's Island was fought on 28 June 1776, when a British fleet under Sir Peter Parker attacked the unfinished palmetto-log fort on Sullivan's Island guarding Charleston harbour. The spongy palmetto logs absorbed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a> fire, and the defenders under William Moultrie badly damaged the ships, forcing the British to withdraw. The fort was renamed Fort Moultrie, and the palmetto became a symbol of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-carolina">South Carolina</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-sullivans-island.jpg" alt="Battle of Sullivan's Island" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johannes Oertel · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Sullivans_Island.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
